 # Multi-Identity Embedding
 ## Overview
-Multi-Identity Embedding is a method for identifying contributing users in collaborative Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) training by embedding customized hidden information about specific clusters of training views [S1]. It solves the problem of scalable attribution in multi-user scenarios by allowing a single NeRF model to hide distinct identities for different spatial regions without requiring model retraining for each new watermark [S1]. Unlike prior approaches that embed only a single global watermark, this method assigns identity information to specific clusters of anchor views, preventing false positives for unmarked identities [S1]. It builds on [StegaNeRF Training Algorithm](16783-steganerf-training-algorithm.md).
+Multi-Identity Embedding is a method for identifying contributing users in collaborative Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) training by embedding customized hidden information about specific clusters of training views [S1]. It solves the problem of scalable attribution in multi-user scenarios by allowing a single NeRF model to hide distinct identities for different spatial regions without requiring model retraining for each new watermark [S1]. Unlike prior approaches that embed only a single global watermark, this method assigns identity information to specific clusters of anchor views, preventing false positives for unmarked identities [S1]. It builds on [StegaNeRF Training Algorithm](16783-steganerf-training-algorithm.md) [S1].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A collection of user-uploaded training images with camera poses [S1].
-*   **Output:** A NeRF model with a modified classifier network capable of recovering specific contributor identities based on the rendering viewpoint [S1].
+*   **Input:** A collection of user-uploaded training images with associated camera poses [S1].
+*   **Output:** A trained NeRF model with a modified classifier network capable of recovering specific contributor identities conditioned on the rendering viewpoint [S1].
 
